operty can be leveraged to address health issues.","context":"4/ treat and slow the deposition of fibrosis in the kidney in the setting of progressive kidney disease; and","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":53,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001171843-26-005562","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000117184326005562/exh_992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f.bin","sha256":"6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f"}},{"id":"f32f490ee3a1f70ceb71b346212689e49307653e4749e8b63b48d4570efc541d","quote":"We believe that our technology is underpinned by well-established research and insights into the underlying biology of aberrant purine metabolism, chronically high serum uric acid and its health consequences. Our aim is to advance a novel proprietary formulation of oxypurinol, a uric acid lowering agent that works by effectively inhibiting xanthine oxidase. We are developing product candidates that include new or existing drugs that can be adapted to address disease indications where aberrant purine metabolism and/or elevated uric acid is a common denominator, including gout, polycystic kidney disease, pre-diabetes, insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome, diabetes, diabetic nephropathy, and infection. We are focused on building a pipeline of assets to address the unmet medical needs of patients with a variety of serious or life-threatening diseases using our innovative formulation of oxypurinol, and in combination with uric acid lowering agents - a pipeline-in-a-product strategy supported by our intellectual property, established exclusive manufacturing agreements, and proposed clinical trials with experienced clinicians. Our pipeline includes additional new chemical entities with beneficial pharmacologic properties able to decrease inflammatory status specifically as accompanied by kidney disease progression and harmful accumulation of kidney fibrosis.","context":"5/ identify other opportunities where our existing and new intellectual property can be leveraged to address health issues.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":54,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001171843-26-005562","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000117184326005562/exh_992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f.bin","sha256":"6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f"}},{"id":"24e1e0e19f6ffd1e775edb5c340a37e0b0d58a3b67d7794b26eac4caeb777654","quote":"Our four current unique product development programs are:","context":"acid and its health consequences. Our aim is to advance a novel proprietary formulation of oxypurinol, a uric acid lowering agent that works by effectively inhibiting xanthine oxidase. We are developing product candidates that include new or existing drugs that can be adapted to address disease indications where aberrant purine metabolism and/or elevated uric acid is a common denominator, including gout, polycystic kidney disease, pre-diabetes, insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome, diabetes, diabetic nephropathy, and infection. We are focused on building a pipeline of assets to address the unmet medical needs of patients with a variety of serious or life-threatening diseases using our innovative formulation of oxypurinol, and in combination with uric acid lowering agents - a pipeline-in-a-product strategy supported by our intellectual property, established exclusive manufacturing agreements, and proposed clinical trials with experienced clinicians. Our pipeline includes additional new chemical entities with beneficial pharmacologic properties able to decrease inflammatory status specifically as accompanied by kidney disease progression and harmful accumulation of kidney fibrosis.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":55,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001171843-26-005562","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000117184326005562/exh_992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f.bin","sha256":"6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f"}},{"id":"8ee444f3323b83cf6acc1aaa484d39ed9e46f423fcb3461a8cff7884190a49ef","quote":"·XRx-026, a program for the treatment of gout;","context":"Our four current unique product development programs are:","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":56,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001171843-26-005562","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000117184326005562/exh_992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f.bin","sha256":"6110f53622c16cc0be27a7212189720b759e50e2c048a7001021fda2b04baf6f"}},{"id":"0810fd80db56c5aea048ad145464092a4e192265c82f6ae626b5aa7493e3b9dc","quote":"·XRx-008, a program for the treatment of ADPKD;","context":"·XRx-026, a program for the treatment of gout;","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":57,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001171843-26-005562","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001729214","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1729214/000117184326005562/exh_992.htm","rawPath":"